Experiment 1 – Git and GitHub Essentials
1. Aim
To perform basic Git operations such as repository initialization, file tracking, committing, branching, merging, and pushing changes to GitHub.
2. New names
Item	Name
Project folder	git-lab-exam
GitHub repository	git-lab-exam
Main branch	main
Feature branch	feature
GitHub username	azcruze
File	index.html

3. Procedure
1. Create a project folder named git-lab-exam.
2. Navigate into the folder.
3. Initialize the Git repository.
4. Check the repository status.
5. Create an HTML file named index.html.
6. Add the file to the staging area.
7. Commit the changes.
8. Rename the default branch to main.
9. Create a new empty GitHub repository named git-lab-exam.
10. Connect the local repository to GitHub.
11. Push the local repository to GitHub.
12. Create a feature branch.
13. Modify the HTML file and commit the changes.
14. Switch to the main branch.
15. Merge the feature branch into main.
16. Push the updated changes to GitHub.
17. Verify the repository on GitHub.
4. Complete commands – Copy and execute
Step 1 – Create project folder
mkdir git-lab-exam
cd git-lab-exam


Step 2 – Initialize Git
git init
git status


Step 3 – Create HTML file
notepad index.html


Paste this code:

<html>
<head>
    <title>Git Lab Examination</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Welcome to Git and GitHub</h1>
    <p>DevOps Lab Experiment 1</p>
</body>
</html>



Save and close Notepad.

Step 4 – Add and commit files
git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit"


Step 5 – Rename branch
git branch -M main


Step 6 – Create GitHub repository

Open GitHub – Create a new repository.

Create the repository with these details:
- Repository name: git-lab-exam
- Owner: azcruze
- Visibility: Public or Private
- Do not select Add a README file.
- Do not add a .gitignore or license.
Click Create repository.

Step 7 – Connect local repository to GitHub
git remote add origin https://github.com/azcruze/git-lab-exam.git
git remote -v


Step 8 – Push files to GitHub
git push -u origin main


If GitHub asks you to authenticate, complete the sign-in in the browser or use the authentication method provided.

Step 9 – Create feature branch
git checkout -b feature


Step 10 – Modify the HTML file
notepad index.html


Replace the existing HTML with:

<html>
<head>
    <title>Git Lab Examination</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Welcome to Git and GitHub</h1>
    <p>DevOps Lab Experiment 1</p>
    <h2>Feature Branch Successfully Created</h2>
</body>
</html>



Save and close Notepad.

Step 11 – Add and commit the changes
git add .
git commit -m "Added feature"


Step 12 – Switch to main branch
git checkout main


Step 13 – Merge feature branch
git merge feature


Step 14 – Push updated changes
git push


Step 15 – Verify
git status
git branch
git log --oneline


Open your repository:
azcruze/git-lab-examYou should see index.html and the latest commits.
5. Expected output
- Git repository initialized successfully.
- HTML file created and committed.
- Main and feature branches created.
- Feature branch successfully merged into main.
- Changes pushed to GitHub.
- Repository and files visible on GitHub.
6. Result
Git operations including initialization, staging, committing, branching, merging, and pushing were successfully performed using Git and GitHub.
7. Memory tip
Remember this order
Create → Init → Add → Commit → Main → Remote → Push → Feature → Commit → Merge → Push → Verify
